Z||000013||Oreif||02-26-2000||12:32 AM||||MM ~ sorry about the MonkeyMobile. Here is somthing you can try. Take a socket and a big ratchet or a breaker bar and using the bolt on the crankshaft turn the engine BACKWARDS maybe 1/4 turn (if it moves) then remove spark plugs and squirt a SMALL amount of oil into them. Then find out why the oil left, fill crankcase with oil again and it might run again. We had an old car that did the same thing and the piston ring jammed it up. By rotating engine backwards we free'd it up and it ran again! Although the cylinder was scored from the bad ring it still ran for another year or so.||||reg||1
