Z||000020||Monkeyman||02-27-2000||06:38 AM||||I tried turning the motor over with a breaker bar last night.  No luck.  It's toast.  For what it will cost to replace the Duke, I can get my GT and get her running.  I guess I'll work on that instead.  Anybody know if you can drop the cradle without using an overhead hoist to lift the body?  I'm sure I've read about it here, but I can't seem to find the info by doing a search.||||reg||1
Z||000021||William Federle||02-27-2000||07:56 AM||||At the V8 archie website under "archisms" there's a writeup on engine removal without a hoist. I think there's a dimension that you have to get the top of the rear wheel wells up above the floor (supporting the frame with jackstands) and then you lower the cradle somehow with a floor jack. Good Luck.||||reg||1
