Z||000023||batboy||02-27-2000||09:41 AM||||Hahaha, the whole dang Fiero weighs less than 1-1/2 tons, those jackstands will be ok. You'll only need to support the back half of the car anyway. Once the cradle's out, there ain't much weight left over.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Monkeyman||02-27-2000||01:53 PM||||bat--That's kinda what I thought, but I didn't  know if a better rating was recommended for safety.  Any idea what the cradle (incl motor/tranny) weighs in at?||||reg||1
Z||000025||b_b_a_d||02-28-2000||12:55 AM||||Actually, I can give a few choice words of wisdom in this department.  <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86_cradle.jpg">   <BR>The wife and I actually hoisted up the back end of the car.  Honestly, I don't know how you could remove the cradle any other way.  It required more clearance than either of us anticipated for the car to clear the cradle enough to pull the engine/cradle out.<BR>(Note the top of the plenum assembly about the same height as shars waist.)<P>Wish I had a picture to show you the nose of the car only an inch from the ground at a 45+ degree angle.<P>Now as far as jack stands go, don't underestimate the weight of the car with or without the engine.  Shar and I had the stands to close to center and boy howdy did she start swingin like a seesaw.  Now as far as using a 2 ton(+) jack to hoist the cradle... be forwarned...  DON'T DO IT!!!  One isn't enough, and I even question the stability of two.  Shar and I modified an engine stand being it had wheels... (Sort of an extended pallet) to support the cradle.)and had two 2 1/2 ton jacks to support  the extension.  I still wasn't comfortable with the set up, but it was pretty solid.  If you have the means, a pallet jack is the best means to support the cradle.  Put a couple of 4x4s down for cross support and come under the car from the side.  That will give you plenty of clearance and height when you go to put it back in not to mention making things much easier!!!  Luckily I had access to my previous employers pallet jack with his blessings when he heard it was for the Fiero.  The pallet jack is pretty manuverable not to mention it allows for a little more control than trying to center and lower the car back on the cradle with just an engine hoist.  <P>Best of luck!!!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just ask if you want to hear about our little escapade...  LOL!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Real_Mechanics.jpg">   <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 02-28-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000026||Monkeyman||02-28-2000||05:57 AM||||b_b_a_d--I emailed you.<P>Yesterday was a very sad day in Fierodom.  I finally decided that the Monkeymobile was truely dead.  I had a mechanic come over to the house to peek under the Monkeymobiles' hood.  He tinkered around with it for about a 1/2 hour before he decided that there wasn't anything to be done other than replacing the motor.  <P>As some of you know, I have purchased an '85 GT (still needs to be picked up).  It needs a new motor and a freshing up of the interior.  (I'm sure the suspension could use a good going-over, too.)  I decided to start to gut the M/mobile.  I need some of the parts for the '85.  The M/mobile cried.  I almost did.  (This is/was my very 1st Fiero.)  You can't imagine how difficult it was to remove parts of my beloved car.  (I don't mean physically.  Most of the parts came out fairly easily.)  <P>On a good note, I've found that alot of parts will do just fine in the '85.  The headliner needs recovered, but the foam is actually in good shape with no cracks, and I got the wiring for the 3rd brake light (that was a real b***h to remove!).  I even got some ideas for some mods.  (Anyone know where I can get a reasonably cheap backup camera-found in alot of larger RVs?)<P>I'll quit being long-winded, but you guys are part of my family and I had to talk to someone.  As FD says, "Thanx for the space."||||reg||1
Z||000027||sdm1964||02-28-2000||06:43 AM||||Just leave the keys and the title in the front seat i will be buy next week to pick it up. Kidding, sorry to hear about the car, bad deal. I hope it all works out for you.||||reg||14
Z||000028||b_b_a_d||02-28-2000||04:09 PM||||Shar and I were talking bout the motor locking up and...  We came to the conclusion that your best bet would be to take a breaker bar and crank the pulley counterclockwise... or from the back of the car pull it toward you.  If it is still to stiff to pull, don't be afraid to put on an extension for more leverage.  You don't really have to worry bout doing much more damage to the engine as this is sort of a last resort.  Don't be afraid to put your body weight into it!  Just don't get hurt!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>If anyone else wants to put there 2 cents in, now is the time!  If 75000 people put there 2 cents in, Monkeyman would have $1500 dollars for the new motor...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Just a thought.  LOL!<p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 02-28-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000029||Raydar||02-28-2000||05:02 PM||||MM... Just for grins, make sure that the starter pinion gear is not jammed in the flywheel ring gear. I had a car once that that happened to. Locked it up tighter than Dick's hatband. Wouldn't even turn over when I rolled the car down the hill, and dumped the clutch. (Based on your previous posts, I really doubt that this is the case, but ya' never know. Good luck.)||||reg||1
Z||000030||Monkeyman||02-28-2000||08:25 PM||||sdm1964--Thanx for the "offer", but I'll never get rid of the Monkeymobile.  It may be in parts, but it'll always be in the way.  (Ummm...I mean, in my driveway.)<P>b_b_a_d--Thanx, but I already tried that.  My mechanic friend got some of his tools.  We had about 6 feet of pipe and a total of almost 500 lbs pulling on it and it still wouldn't budge.  BTW--Buy Craftsman.<P>Raydar--The mechanic tried/checked something with the starter.  I have to assume that's what it was.  I appreciate the idea, though.<P>I was thinking that now would be a good time to try and duplicate Eddy Snauuws dash.  I have the dash in the garage right now.  I wonder...?  <P>||||reg||1
